@startuml component-diagram
title Smart City Waste Management System - Component Diagram

left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

actor Citizen
actor Driver
actor "Admin / Municipal Officer" as Admin
actor "Disposal Facility Operator" as Operator

package "Presentation Layer" {
  component "Web Frontend" as Web
}

package "Application / Service Layer" {
  component "Auth & User Service" as Auth
  component "Request Service" as Request
  component "Fleet Service" as Fleet
  component "Facility Service" as Facility
  component "Route Optimization Engine" as Route
  component "Notification & Reporting Service" as Notify
}

package "External Map Service" {
  component "Map Service\n(OpenStreetMap)" as Map
}

database "Database\n(PostgreSQL)" as DB

Citizen --> Web
Driver --> Web
Admin --> Web
Operator --> Web

Web --> Auth : Authentication
Web --> Request : Collection requests
Web --> Fleet : Vehicle management
Web --> Facility : Facility management
Web --> Route : Route generation
Web --> Notify : Dashboard / reports

Auth --> DB : Users, roles, audit log
Request --> DB : Requests / status
Fleet --> DB : Vehicles / capacity
Facility --> DB : Facilities / capacity
Route --> DB : Routes / stops
Notify --> DB : Reports / status data

Request --> Map : Location lookup
Facility --> Map : Facility locations
Route --> Map : Distance / route map
Web --> Map : Map display

Request --> Notify : Status changes
Route --> Fleet : Vehicle capacity
Route --> Facility : Facility eligibility
Route --> Request : Approved requests
Route --> Notify : Route / stop updates

note bottom of Auth
SCW-SEC-006: Admin audit logging
end note

note bottom of Web
SCW-SEC-003: HTTPS (TLS 1.2+)
end note

note bottom of Route
SCW-F-040 to SCW-F-044
SCW-NF-001: Route generation performance
end note

note right of DB
Persistent storage for system data
end note

note bottom
Shared requirements:
SCW-NF-002, SCW-NF-003,
SCW-NF-005 and SCW-SO-2
apply to all services.
end note

@enduml
